Subject: [PATCH 03899/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE B1 (INFRA
 -- reserved slot 1) -- ship the PERCEPTION-QUALITY CI-metric + the OFF-PATH
 discrimination metric that guard the A1 perception lever: (1) a
 LOO-discrimination gate that LOCKS the order-1-vs-relational perception
 measurement (cross_game_features_v2 LOO-AUROC=0.503=chance baseline vs the
 richer representation) so a perception change is mechanically trackable and
 cannot silently regress to chance; (2) an OFF-PATH discrimination metric -- a
 representation's held-out discrimination measured on the LIVE off-path search
 distribution (not winning paths only), so the offline->live bridge gap (the
 .425-B2 finding) is a measurable number, not an after-the-fact surprise; (3)
 a perception-quality floor. Unit tests green. verifier_is_oracle:false.

